LICENCE HISTORY
---------------
Up to and including 0.38.0    MIT
0.39.0 to 0.42.1              GPL-3.0-or-later
From 0.43.0                   AGPL-3.0-only

Each change applies to new releases only. A grant already made is not revoked,
and it cannot be. A copy obtained under MIT stays under MIT for its recipient,
and a copy obtained under GPL-3.0-or-later stays under GPL-3.0-or-later,
permanently.

LumenPOS moved to the AGPL because it is software people use over a network.
Under the GPL, a modified LumenPOS could be offered to shops as a hosted service
without its changes ever being shared, because running a service is not
distribution. Under the AGPL, anyone who runs a modified version for users over
a network must offer those users its complete source code.


COMPATIBILITY WITH ERPNEXT AND FRAPPE
-------------------------------------
LumenPOS calls ERPNext's own code directly (loyalty points, POS invoice
consolidation and the credit note builder, see lumenpos/erpnext_compat.py).
ERPNext is licensed under version 3 of the GNU General Public License.

The two licences are designed to be combined. Section 13 of the GPLv3 permits
linking or combining a work it covers with a work licensed under version 3 of
the GNU Affero General Public License into a single combined work, and section
13 of the AGPLv3 gives the same permission from the other side. Each part keeps
its own licence, and the network interaction requirement of the AGPLv3 applies
to the combination as such.

Frappe Framework is licensed under MIT, which is compatible with both.

AGPL-3.0 is accepted on the Frappe Cloud Marketplace, which requires apps to be
open source and compatible with MIT or the GPL.
